              <p class="ex-a-line"><b class="lbl">Answer.</b> The graph and the list:</p>
              <div class="st-pic"><div><GraphFig g={store4.g} label="The graph drawn from the matrix" /></div><div><Fragment set:html={listHtml(store4.g)} /></div></div>
              <p class="ex-a-line">No outgoing edges: <span class="ans">D</span></p>
            </div>
            <p>D's row is all 0, so no arrows leave D, though {inCount(store4.g, 'D')} arrive (column D). Usual mistakes are drawing arrows backwards (row = from, column = to) or leaving out the arrowheads.</p>
          </div>
